{"data":{"cross":"d63c7b6e0237dff374a3d9cb47f782d7bec49ebba08c6665751aa05851a889f6","ends":[0,61,38]},"findings":[{"column":1,"line":1,"message":"[BE_SPEC_PLACEMENT] be/apps/cli/src/app.module.spec.ts is a spec outside the test layers (slot be.app.cli); a unit spec is <name>.service.spec.ts beside its service and an integration, e2e or contract spec sits under be/src/tests/{integration,e2e,contract}; an operational script or a tool carries no spec","path":"be/apps/cli/src/app.module.spec.ts","rule":"starci-be/spec-placement"},{"column":1,"line":1,"message":"`app.module.spec.ts` is a unit spec of something that carries no unit-tested logic here. A unit spec sits beside a `<name>.<role>.ts` of a spec-required role (a service, a cli command of `be/src/features/cli`) or of a logic role (`ruleParams.be.logicRoles`: policy, client, guard, mapper, ...) inside the logic of `be/src/modules/**`, or a logic file its slot declares (`logic`), where every file owes 100 per file; a feature file (handler, resolver, controller, consumer, processor, step, ...) is thin (BE_FEATURE_THIN) and is proven by the integration and e2e flows, and an entity, module or composition is declaration. Delete this spec and move any business rule it checks into a service, policy or mapper of `be/src/modules/**`.","path":"be/apps/cli/src/app.module.spec.ts","rule":"starci-be/unit-test-colocated"},{"column":98,"line":38,"message":"`isGlobal: true` outside `be/apps/<app>/src/app.module.ts` and its `compose/<area>.ts` groups makes a module global from the wrong place. Only the app registers a capability, once, with `isGlobal: true`; here keep the module's own default.","path":"be/apps/cli/src/app.module.spec.ts","rule":"starci-be/is-global-only-in-app"}],"hash":"0e24bcea2d65c4e4e9c6e15692a3fc9ed918909d5e910ab52d883806cfbadc29","path":"apps/cli/src/app.module.spec.ts","step":"eslint"}
